   "notes": "No ON-only signal survived: filter 2 and filter 3 are empty at both S/N 10 and S/N 5. The strongest hits are a steady, non-drifting tone at 1420.000001 MHz (|drift| <= 0.015 Hz/s, S/N 25-36) seen in all six scans, three ON and three OFF, plus a weaker line near 1419.9866 MHz also in ON and OFF scans. A tone sitting at a round-number frequency, not drifting and present off-source is typical of local/terrestrial RFI; the transmitter was not identified. The natural 21-cm hydrogen line (1420.406 MHz) is a broad emission feature (tens to hundreds of kHz wide), not a narrowband drifting signal, so this search is not sensitive to it. Positive control: the synthetic 0.37 Hz/s tone injected into the ON scans was flagged by find_event_pipeline as a filter-3 event at the right drift (0.379 Hz/s, S/N 49), but the saved event table lists only the first-ON hit (in_n_ons = 2), so the cadence logic recovered it only partly; treat the pipeline's completeness on this channel as not fully verified. Run on 12 Oct 2026 (~8 min search + injection test). Breakthrough Listen's own 1-12 GHz analysis of 3I/ATLAS found only terrestrial RFI (arXiv:2512.19763)."
